[{"category":"section","location":"#DiscreteIntegration.jl","page":"Home","text":"Numerical integration of discrete data: sampled values y on a uniform grid (spacing Δx) or a non-uniform grid x. Supports the trapezoidal rule and Simpson's rule, as definite and as cumulative integrals. Elements are loaded only once, so lazy arrays are supported.","title":"DiscreteIntegration.jl"},{"category":"section","location":"#Installation","page":"Home","text":"using Pkg\nPkg.add(\"DiscreteIntegration\")","title":"Installation"},{"category":"section","location":"#Quick-start","page":"Home","text":"using DiscreteIntegration\n\nx = range(0, 1; length = 101)\ny = x .^ 2\n\nintegrate(x, y)                  # trapezoidal rule (default)\n0.33335000000000004\n\nusing DiscreteIntegration\n\nx = range(0, 1; length = 101)\ny = x .^ 2\n\nintegrate(step(x), y, Simpson())   # uniform grid, Simpson\n0.33333333333333337\n\nusing DiscreteIntegration\n\nx = range(0, 1; length = 5)\ny = x .^ 2\n\ncumul_integrate(x, y, Simpson())   # cumulative integral\n5-element Vector{Float64}:\n 0.0\n 0.005208333333333333\n 0.041666666666666664\n 0.140625\n 0.33333333333333337","title":"Quick start"},{"category":"section","location":"#Methods","page":"Home","text":"Method Exact for polynomials up to degree\nTrapezoidal() 1\nSimpson(), non-uniform grid x 2\nSimpson(), uniform grid Δx 3","title":"Methods"},{"category":"section","location":"#API","page":"Home","text":"","title":"API"},{"category":"module","location":"#DiscreteIntegration.DiscreteIntegration","page":"Home","text":"DiscreteIntegration\n\nNumerical integration of discrete data, given as sampled values y on an uneven grid x or an even grid with spacing Δx.\n\nExports:\n\nintegrate: definite integral over all points\ncumul_integrate: cumulative integral, returns a new vector\ncumul_integrate!: cumulative integral, inplace\nTrapezoidal, Simpson: integration methods\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"DiscreteIntegration.DiscreteIntegration"},{"category":"type","location":"#DiscreteIntegration.Simpson","page":"Home","text":"Simpson()\n\nIntegration method: Simpson rule. Exact for polynomials up to degree 2 on uneven grids (x, y) and up to degree 3 on even grids (Δx, y). If the number of points is even, the last interval is treated separately:\n\nuneven grid: Cartwright correction\neven grid: Simpson 3/8 rule\n\nRequires at least 3 points.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"DiscreteIntegration.Simpson"},{"category":"type","location":"#DiscreteIntegration.Trapezoidal","page":"Home","text":"Trapezoidal()\n\nIntegration method: trapezoidal rule. Exact for polynomials up to degree 1.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"DiscreteIntegration.Trapezoidal"},{"category":"function","location":"#DiscreteIntegration.cumul_integrate","page":"Home","text":"cumul_integrate(Δx, y, method = Trapezoidal())\n\nComputes the cumulative numerical integral of y for an even grid spacing.\n\nArguments:\n\nΔx::Real: constant spacing of the y values (may be negative)\ny::AbstractVector{<:Real}: vector of y values\nmethod::IntegrationMethod: integration method, Trapezoidal() (default) or Simpson()\n\nReturns:\n\nVector of at least Float64 with the same length as y. The first element is zero, element k is the integral from the first point to point k.\n\nThrows:\n\nArgumentError: if fewer than 2 points (Trapezoidal) or 3 points (Simpson) are given\n\nNotes:\n\nFor Simpson, the second element is computed with the trapezoidal rule.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"DiscreteIntegration.cumul_integrate"},{"category":"function","location":"#DiscreteIntegration.cumul_integrate-2","page":"Home","text":"cumul_integrate(x, y, method = Trapezoidal())\n\nComputes the cumulative numerical integral of y(x). The grid may be uneven.\n\nArguments:\n\nx::AbstractVector{<:Real}: vector or range of x values\ny::AbstractVector{<:Real}: vector of corresponding y values\nmethod::IntegrationMethod: integration method, Trapezoidal() (default) or Simpson()\n\nReturns:\n\nVector of at least Float64 with the same length as y. The first element is zero, element k is the integral from the first point to point k.\n\nThrows:\n\nDimensionMismatch: if x and y differ in length\nArgumentError: if fewer than 2 points (Trapezoidal) or 3 points (Simpson) are given\n\nNotes:\n\nFor Simpson, x must be strictly monotonic.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"DiscreteIntegration.cumul_integrate"},{"category":"function","location":"#DiscreteIntegration.cumul_integrate!","page":"Home","text":"cumul_integrate!(dest, x, y, method = Trapezoidal())\n\nComputes the cumulative numerical integral of y(x) inplace. The grid may be uneven.\n\nArguments:\n\ndest::AbstractVector{<:AbstractFloat}: output vector, same length as y\nx::AbstractVector{<:Real}: vector or range of x values\ny::AbstractVector{<:Real}: vector of corresponding y values\nmethod::IntegrationMethod: integration method, Trapezoidal() (default) or Simpson()\n\nReturns:\n\ndest, with dest[1] = 0 and element k as the integral from the first point to point k\n\nThrows:\n\nDimensionMismatch: if dest, x and y differ in length\nArgumentError: if fewer than 2 points (Trapezoidal) or 3 points (Simpson) are given\n\nNotes:\n\nComputation uses at least Float64 and is rounded to eltype(dest) on write. The caller is responsible for choosing a suitable dest type.\ndest may be identical to x or y. Partially overlapping views are not allowed.\nFor Simpson, x must be strictly monotonic.\nVectors must have contiguous 1D indices.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"DiscreteIntegration.cumul_integrate!"},{"category":"function","location":"#DiscreteIntegration.cumul_integrate!-2","page":"Home","text":"cumul_integrate!(dest, Δx, y, method = Trapezoidal())\n\nComputes the cumulative numerical integral of y inplace for an even grid spacing.\n\nArguments:\n\ndest::AbstractVector{<:AbstractFloat}: output vector, same length as y\nΔx::Real: constant spacing of the y values (may be negative)\ny::AbstractVector{<:Real}: vector of y values\nmethod::IntegrationMethod: integration method, Trapezoidal() (default) or Simpson()\n\nReturns:\n\ndest, with dest[1] = 0 and element k as the integral from the first point to point k\n\nThrows:\n\nDimensionMismatch: if dest and y differ in length\nArgumentError: if fewer than 2 points (Trapezoidal) or 3 points (Simpson) are given\n\nNotes:\n\nComputation uses at least Float64 and is rounded to eltype(dest) on write. The caller is responsible for choosing a suitable dest type.\ndest may be identical to y. Partially overlapping views are not allowed.\nFor Simpson, the second element is computed with the trapezoidal rule.\nVectors must have contiguous 1D indices.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"DiscreteIntegration.cumul_integrate!"},{"category":"function","location":"#DiscreteIntegration.integrate","page":"Home","text":"integrate(Δx, y, method = Trapezoidal())\n\nComputes the numerical integral of y over all points for an even grid spacing.\n\nArguments:\n\nΔx::Real: constant spacing of the y values (may be negative)\ny::AbstractVector{<:Real}: vector of y values\nmethod::IntegrationMethod: integration method, Trapezoidal() (default) or Simpson()\n\nReturns:\n\nscalar of at least Float64\n\nThrows:\n\nArgumentError: if fewer than 2 points (Trapezoidal) or 3 points (Simpson) are given\n\nNotes:\n\nΔx = 0 returns 0.\nElements of y are loaded only once, so lazy arrays are supported.\nVectors must have contiguous 1D indices.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"DiscreteIntegration.integrate"},{"category":"function","location":"#DiscreteIntegration.integrate-2","page":"Home","text":"integrate(x, y, method = Trapezoidal())\n\nComputes the numerical integral of y(x) over all points. The grid may be uneven.\n\nArguments:\n\nx::AbstractVector{<:Real}: vector or range of x values\ny::AbstractVector{<:Real}: vector of corresponding y values\nmethod::IntegrationMethod: integration method, Trapezoidal() (default) or Simpson()\n\nReturns:\n\nscalar of at least Float64\n\nThrows:\n\nDimensionMismatch: if x and y differ in length\nArgumentError: if fewer than 2 points (Trapezoidal) or 3 points (Simpson) are given\n\nNotes:\n\nx may be descending, the integral then changes sign.\nFor Simpson, x must be strictly monotonic (no duplicate x values).\nElements of x and y are loaded only once, so lazy arrays are supported.\nVectors must have contiguous 1D indices.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"DiscreteIntegration.integrate"}]
